# Local development only. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
# .env* is gitignored — never commit a real token.
#
# Pretalx API token, for the reads that are not public: speaker company/role/
# social links, and the talk level. Create one at
#   https://cfp.cloudnativedays.fr/orga/me
# scoped to the event, with read access to `questions` and `answers`.
#
# Without it, `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build` still work — they warn and render
# speakers with no affiliation and a schedule with no level chips. The
# production image sets PRETALX_TOKEN_REQUIRED=1 so a release cannot ship that.
PRETALX_API_TOKEN=

# Override the Pretalx instance (defaults to https://cfp.cloudnativedays.fr).
# PRETALX_BASE_URL=

# Validation fixture for the unreleased-programme path (local / staging only).
# Points an edition at an existing non-public Pretalx event so the authenticated
# preview reader can be exercised before the real event exists. Refused on a
# production build — and the origin resolves as PUBLIC_SITE_URL || production,
# so an UNSET or EMPTY PUBLIC_SITE_URL counts as production and the fixture
# refuses. It has to be told a non-production origin.
#
# Pass all of it INLINE on the one command that wants it. Do NOT add these as
# keys in .env.local: this file is bridged into process.env for `pnpm dev`,
# `pnpm build` AND `pnpm test` (vitest.config.ts calls loadLocalEnv), so a
# PUBLIC_SITE_URL parked here tells every build and every test that it is that
# origin, and a fixture slug parked here makes every ordinary local build reach
# for democon.
#
#   PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:4321 FLAG_OVERRIDES=programme=on \
#     PRETALX_PREVIEW_SLUG=democon PRETALX_PREVIEW_EDITION=2027 pnpm build
